{# ------------------------------------ C THE ONE RESEARCH NAVIGATION INSTRUMENT #}
<section class="think" id="how-we-think" aria-labelledby="think-h2">
  <div class="think-inner">
    <div class="think-head">
      <div class="think-title">
        <p class="mod-label">How we think</p>
        <h2 class="think-h2" id="think-h2">Advice your team can act on.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="think-intro">We connect what people need with the decisions, responsibilities and practical changes your team can make.</p>
    </div>

    <ol class="principles" id="principles">
      <li class="principle" data-node="1">
        <span class="p-idx" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <h3>Start with people, not a platform</h3>
        <p>We look at what people are trying to do and where they get stuck. The answer may involve an existing channel, better documentation or a useful connection, rather than another place to gather.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="principle" data-node="2">
        <span class="p-idx" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <h3>Understand before committing</h3>
        <p>We investigate needs and behaviour before recommending an approach. The result may be a program design, different incentives, clearer coordination or a decision to stop an initiative.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="principle" data-node="3">
        <span class="p-idx" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <h3>Make ownership clear</h3>
        <p>Recommendations need people who can carry them forward. We consider responsibilities, capacity and the handovers needed to make the approach usable by your team.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="principle"><span class="p-idx" aria-hidden="true">04</span><h3>Use AI for a practical purpose</h3><p>We use AI to support analysis and consider where it can help people find knowledge or complete a task. We assess it against the problem at hand, with human judgment responsible for the recommendation.</p></li>
    </ol>

  </div>
</section>

